      "title": "US midterm elections 2026 live: Americans go to the polls to decide control of Congress",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-live-updates-voting",
      "description": "<p>Voters are casting ballots across the US in a referendum on Donald Trump’s agenda</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US email</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/02/what-are-midterm-elections\">What are the races to watch and why do they matter?</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-polls-close-what-time\">Midterm elections 2026: what time do the polls close today?</a></p></li></ul><p>It has just gone past 06:30 in <strong>North Carolina</strong>, <strong>Ohio</strong> and <strong>West Virginia</strong> where polls have now opened.</p><p>Here are some of the key voter issues shaping the US midterm elections:</p><p><strong>The economy</strong>: Despite Trump’s 2024 campaign pledge to tackle affordability issues, the economy consistently ranks as voters’ top concern.</p><p><strong>Iran</strong>: Trump’s decision to go to war with the Tehran regime has exacerbated economic worries. Iran’s retaliatory decision to close the strait of Hormuz has driven up gasoline prices for US motorists. It also represents a breach of his pledge to end the US’s supposed addiction to “forever wars”.</p><p><strong>Immigration</strong>: Enforcement and closing the border remains a signature issue for Trump. He repeatedly boasts of the impact of his closure of the southern border as one of his biggest achievements, making comparisons with the performance of Joe Biden.</p><p><strong>AI and datacenters:</strong> AI has emerged as a key campaign issue, with surveys showing a majority of voters holding negative views on it, even as Trump champions its development and attempts to rename it “super intelligence”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-live-updates-voting\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T18:39:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Americans head to polls in midterm elections seen as referendum on Trump",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-americans-vote",
      "description": "<p>Control of the Senate and House of Representatives, both currently held by the Republicans, is at stake</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-live-updates-voting\">US midterm elections 2026: latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Americans are heading to the polls today in US midterm elections widely seen as a referendum on Donald Trump’s second presidency and a chance for opponents to rein in his untrammeled power.</p><p>Democrats and Republicans have scrambled in recent days to deliver their final pitches to voters, with control of the US Senate and House of Representatives – both currently held by the Republicans – at stake. Also on the ballot are 36 governor’s races, as well as control of state legislatures, sheriff’s races and ballot measures.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/03/midterm-elections-americans-vote\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T15:17:04"
    },
